hi all:
I use kernel 3.8.13 and when I unplug usb2.0 HD from ehci.
Some times it will keep printing below message

[ 1][   52.079671] sd 3:0:0:0: [sdb] Unhandled error code
[ 1][   52.079678] sd 3:0:0:0: [sdb]
[ 1][   52.079682] Result: hostbyte=0x07 driverbyte=0x00
.........................

what makes me curious are:
1. logical disconnect already shows up. That mean
"us->pusb_dev->state" is changed to USB_STATE_NOTATTACHED
2.why scsi cannot get #1 usb state to turn off keeping send command?
3. Is there any debug opion/config I can open to tell whether scsi
layer trap in some loop?
4. is it due to usb_disconnect called by khubd to late?
    But we have set us->pusb_dev->state as USB_STATE_NOTATTACHED in
hub_port_logical_disconnect, which should prevent further command even
usb_stor_disconnect is not called, right?

-- 
Regards,

